Original commit body from e9f810e:

For flat repos where all files are at the root level (like qemu-sgabios),
the Structure section now shows source files even if they don't have
detected symbols.

Previously, only files with symbols were collected for the Structure tree.
This meant that `.h` files with only `#define` macros, assembly files, and
other source files without parseable symbols would be hidden under
"[and N other items]" even when there was room to show them.

New step 5b in `_collect_important_files`:
- Scans root-level files for source file patterns (*.c, *.h, *.py, etc.)
- Adds them AFTER files with symbols (preserving importance ordering)
- Respects max_root_files limit (default 5)

Example improvement for qemu-sgabios:
  Before: Makefile, csum8.c, [and 6 other items]
  After:  Makefile, csum8.c, sgabios.h, [and 5 other items]
